---

<article class="glass-card rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-8 text-slate-300">
  {/* Header Section */}
  <div>
    <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight mb-3">
      Comprehensive Guide to PDF Invoicing & Client Billing
    </h2>
    <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      An invoice is more than a request for payment—it is a legally binding accounting document that establishes payment terms, itemizes services rendered, and protects your business cash flow. Generating clean, professional PDF invoices ensures faster payment processing by corporate accounting departments and reduces payment disputes.
    </p>
  </div>

  {/* Formula / Calculation Breakdown Box */}
  <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-slate-950 border border-slate-800 space-y-3">
    <h3 class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-indigo-400">
      Invoice Total Calculation Formula
    </h3>
    <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-indigo-950/40 border border-indigo-500/30 text-center font-mono text-sm sm:text-base text-white font-bold">
      Grand Total = ∑ (Quantity × Unit Price) + Total Tax Amount - Applicable Discounts
    </div>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
      Each line item subtotal is computed by multiplying item quantity by unit price. Applicable sales tax or VAT is calculated per line item or applied to the net invoice subtotal before adding shipping or subtracting retainers.
    </p>
  </div>

  {/* Real-World Worked Numerical Example */}
  <div class="space-y-4">
    <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">
      Worked Numerical Example: Web Development Project Invoice
    </h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      Suppose a freelance software engineer completes a web redesign project consisting of custom design work, API integration, and ongoing maintenance:
    </p>

    <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-slate-800">
      <table class="w-full text-left text-xs border-collapse font-mono">
        <thead class="bg-slate-950 text-slate-200 border-b border-slate-800 uppercase text-[10px]">
          <tr>
            <th class="p-3">Line Item Description</th>
            <th class="p-3 text-center">Qty</th>
            <th class="p-3 text-right">Unit Price</th>
            <th class="p-3 text-right">Tax (10%)</th>
            <th class="p-3 text-right">Subtotal</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-800/60 text-slate-300">
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3 font-sans">UI/UX Design Mockups</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-center">1</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-right">$1,200.00</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-right">$120.00</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-right text-white font-bold">$1,200.00</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3 font-sans">Frontend React Development</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-center">20 hrs</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-right">$85.00</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-right">$170.00</td>
            <td class="p-3 text-right text-white font-bold">$1,700.00</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-950 border border-slate-800 space-y-1.5 text-xs">
      <div class="flex justify-between text-slate-400">
        <span>Net Subtotal:</span>
        <span class="font-mono text-slate-200 font-bold">$2,900.00</span>
      </div>
      <div class="flex justify-between text-slate-400">
        <span>Sales Tax / VAT (10%):</span>
        <span class="font-mono text-slate-200 font-bold">$290.00</span>
      </div>
      <div class="flex justify-between text-base font-extrabold text-indigo-400 border-t border-slate-800 pt-2">
        <span>Total Amount Due:</span>
        <span class="font-mono">$3,190.00</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {/* Practical Freelance Advice */}
  <div class="space-y-3">
    <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">
      Best Practices for Freelancers & Small Business Owners
    </h3>
    <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      <li><strong>Always State Explicit Payment Terms:</strong> Use clear due dates (e.g., "Net 14" or "Due October 15, 2026") rather than vague phrases like "Due upon receipt".</li>
      <li><strong>Include Purchase Order (P.O.) Numbers:</strong> Large corporate clients require a valid P.O. number to match accounts payable invoices with approved budgets.</li>
      <li><strong>Provide Multiple Payment Methods:</strong> List wire transfer routing numbers, ACH payment links, or Stripe checkout links directly in the invoice notes.</li>
      <li><strong>Maintain Sequential Invoice Numbering:</strong> Use a standardized prefix format like <code>INV-2026-001</code> to simplify annual tax audits and bookkeeping.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  {/* Frequently Asked Questions */}
  <div class="space-y-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-800">
    <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">
      Frequently Asked Questions About PDF Invoicing
    </h3>
    <div class="space-y-4 text-sm">
      <div class="border-b border-slate-800/80 pb-3">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-white mb-1">What mandatory details must be on a professional invoice?</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-400">Every valid invoice must include your business name, contact info, client business details, a unique invoice ID number, issuance date, payment due date, itemized description of goods/services, subtotal, tax rate, and total amount due.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="border-b border-slate-800/80 pb-3">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-white mb-1">Why should I send invoices in PDF format instead of Word or Excel?</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-400">PDFs preserve strict formatting across operating systems and devices, prevent unauthorized editing of amounts or bank details, and print cleanly for physical accounting records.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="border-b border-slate-800/80 pb-3">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-white mb-1">What is the difference between Net 15, Net 30, and Due on Receipt?</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-400">"Net 15" means full payment is expected within 15 calendar days from the invoice issuance date. "Net 30" extends the payment window to 30 days. "Due on Receipt" requires payment immediately upon delivery of the invoice.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="border-b border-slate-800/80 pb-3">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-white mb-1">Are my client invoice details stored on your servers?</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-400">No. SimpleInvoiceTools operates 100% client-side inside your browser. Your financial figures, client names, and invoice data are never uploaded, logged, or saved to any external database.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="pb-1">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-white mb-1">How can I invoice international clients in different currencies?</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-400">Our free invoice generator supports 10 global currencies (USD, EUR, GBP, AUD, CAD, JPY, INR, etc.). Simply select your target currency from the dropdown menu to format all itemized subtotals automatically.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</article>
